# A hexadecimal immediate is read at its instruction's width, as the
# signed value of its bits: 0xFFFFFFFF in a `setp.lt.s32` is -1, so the
# loop counting from -4 runs 3 trips, and 0xFFFFFFF0 in an `add.s32` is
# -16, which `mul.wide.s32` widens to param_0 + 4·n - 64. An unsigned
# reading takes the same bits as unsigned: a `cvt.u64.u32` of 0xFFFFFFF0
# is 2^32 - 16 (ptxas 13.4: `UIADD3 ... -0x10`, `UIADD3.X ... URZ`), and
# a `setp.lt.u32` of %tid.x and 0xFFFFFFFC holds on every thread. The
# `setp.lt.u32` latch of 0xFFFFFFFC reads 2^32 - 4 trips, refused
# (PLAN.md): its counter's `add.s32` reaches it, past `.s32`. A
# `selp.u32` of 0xFFFFFFC0 and 0 by %tid.x's bit 4 is -64 + 64·bit 4.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/hex_immediates.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_1: // loop: trips 3 | global per CTA: requested 384 B, unique 4 B, sectors 96 B | warp * × lane * | exec 96/CTA{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r2; // global store [param_0 + 4·param_1 - 64] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB2_1: // loop: trips ? (uniform(%r1@{{[0-9]+}}) is defined in an enclosing loop: `add.s32` leaves 32 bits) | warp * × lane * | exec ?{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [param_0 + 4294967280] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd1], %r1; // [<block 1>] warp * × lane * | exec 32/CTA | global store [param_0] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [4·%tid.x + 64·⌊(%tid.x mod 32)/16⌋ + param_0 - 64] sectors/req 4 (ideal 4){{$}}
